1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Social Studies, Class 5.

2
00:00:03,020 --> 00:00:05,000
Lesson 2: Earth Movement.

3
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:08,860
Learning Objectives.

4
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:13,000
By the end of this chapter,

5
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:15,080
learners will be able to:

6
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,980
Understand that the Earth is spherical.

7
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:21,380
Identify the two types of movements of

8
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:21,860
the Earth.

9
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:24,940
Explain rotation and its effects.

10
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:28,300
Understand revolution and its effects.

11
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:32,080
Learn about different seasons caused by revolution.

12
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:36,060
Define solstices and equinoxes and when they

13
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:36,460
occur.

14
00:00:38,970 --> 00:00:39,860
Start-Up Activity.

15
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:44,900
Take a ball and spin it.

16
00:00:45,580 --> 00:00:46,840
Notice how it moves.

17
00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:50,440
Imagine this is the Earth moving in

18
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:50,840
space.

19
00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:55,360
The Earth moves in two ways—let's explore

20
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:57,260
these movements and their effects!

21
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:01,380
Who proved that the earth is spherical?

22
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:07,840
Many ancient civilizations believed that the Earth

23
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:08,500
was flat.

24
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:12,980
However, Greek philosopher Pythagoras was one of

25
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:15,000
the first to suggest that the Earth

26
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:15,740
is spherical.

27
00:01:16,520 --> 00:01:20,380
Later, Aristotle provided evidence by observing how

28
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:23,300
ships disappear over the horizon and how

29
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:25,300
the Earth's shadow on the Moon is

30
00:01:25,380 --> 00:01:27,180
curved during a lunar eclipse.

31
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:30,900
Ferdinand Magellan's voyage around the world further

32
00:01:30,980 --> 00:01:32,940
confirmed that the Earth is round.

33
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:37,200
The Two Movements of the Earth.

34
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:42,240
The Earth moves in two ways:

35
00:01:43,540 --> 00:01:45,920
Rotation – The Earth spins on its

36
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:47,480
axis around itself.

37
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:51,540
Revolution – The Earth moves around the

38
00:01:51,620 --> 00:01:51,940
Sun.

39
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:54,740
Rotation.

40
00:01:57,260 --> 00:01:59,880
The movement of the Earth around its

41
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:01,960
own axis is called rotation.

42
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:05,380
The earth rotates from west to east.

43
00:02:06,140 --> 00:02:08,980
It completes one full rotation in 24

44
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:09,380
hours.

45
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:12,360
The speed of rotation is faster at

46
00:02:12,440 --> 00:02:14,820
the equator and slower at the poles.

47
00:02:15,660 --> 00:02:17,800
The axis is tilted at an angle

48
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:20,348
of 23.5°.

49
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:22,540
As the Earth is spherical in shape,

50
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:25,060
only one half of the Earth receives

51
00:02:25,140 --> 00:02:26,320
sunlight at a time.

52
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:28,960
Thus, the side of the Earth facing

53
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:30,900
the Sun experience day.

54
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:32,440
On the other hand,

55
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:33,640
the other half,

56
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:35,720
or the part away from the sun,

57
00:02:36,020 --> 00:02:37,220
experiences night.

58
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:39,320
As the Earth rotates,

59
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:42,080
the lighted part moves into the darkness.

60
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:45,420
This rotation causes day and night.

61
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:48,460
Do You Know?

62
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:53,020
The Earth rotates at a speed of

63
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:57,460
1,670 kilometers per hour at the equator,

64
00:02:58,120 --> 00:03:00,064
but we don’t feel it because we’re

65
00:03:00,144 --> 00:03:01,340
moving along with it!

66
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:04,340
Revolution.

67
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:09,560
Revolution is the movement of the Earth

68
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:11,860
around the Sun in a fixed path

69
00:03:11,940 --> 00:03:13,060
called an orbit.

70
00:03:13,740 --> 00:03:15,980
The Earth revolves around the Sun in

71
00:03:16,060 --> 00:03:17,180
an elliptical orbit.

72
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:20,140
It takes three hundred and sixty-five and

73
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:23,180
one quarter days (one year) to complete

74
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:24,180
one revolution.

75
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:27,240
The tilt of the Earth's axis remains

76
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:29,040
the same during revolution.

77
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:32,060
Revolution causes seasonal changes.

78
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:34,740
The revolution of the Earth and the

79
00:03:34,820 --> 00:03:37,440
tilt of its axis cause different seasons:

80
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:41,240
Summer – The hemisphere tilted towards the

81
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,960
Sun experiences summer.

82
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:46,520
Winter – The hemisphere tilted away from

83
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:48,440
the Sun experiences winter.

84
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:52,120
Spring – Occurs between winter and summer

85
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:54,180
when the temperature starts rising.

86
00:03:54,880 --> 00:03:57,580
Autumn – Occurs between summer and winter

87
00:03:57,660 --> 00:03:59,620
when the temperature starts dropping.

88
00:04:02,020 --> 00:04:03,040
Let's Learn More.

89
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:08,400
A day on Earth is actually 23

90
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:10,140
hours, 56 minutes,

91
00:04:10,780 --> 00:04:12,620
not exactly 24 hours,

92
00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:14,960
but we round it off to 24

93
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:17,260
hours because it’s easier to keep track

94
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:17,740
of time.

95
00:04:20,079 --> 00:04:22,299
What is Solstice and When Does It

96
00:04:22,379 --> 00:04:22,699
Occur?

97
00:04:25,379 --> 00:04:26,879
A solstice is a day,

98
00:04:26,959 --> 00:04:29,619
when the sun shines vertically over a

99
00:04:29,699 --> 00:04:33,059
Tropic (both cancer and Capricorn) in the

100
00:04:33,139 --> 00:04:35,539
afternoon and the day is the longest

101
00:04:35,619 --> 00:04:36,699
in that hemisphere.

102
00:04:37,499 --> 00:04:39,259
On the twenty-second of December,

103
00:04:39,779 --> 00:04:41,739
the rays of the sun fall directly

104
00:04:41,819 --> 00:04:43,519
over the Tropic of Capricorn.

105
00:04:44,139 --> 00:04:46,299
This is the longest day in Southern

106
00:04:46,379 --> 00:04:48,119
Hemisphere (summer season),

107
00:04:48,539 --> 00:04:49,959
while in the Northern Hemisphere,

108
00:04:50,039 --> 00:04:52,659
it is the shortest day (winter season).

109
00:04:53,359 --> 00:04:55,379
This is called 'Winter Solstice.

110
00:04:56,179 --> 00:04:57,739
On the twenty-first of June,

111
00:04:58,439 --> 00:05:00,819
sunlight falls vertically over the Tropic of

112
00:05:00,899 --> 00:05:01,219
Cancer.

113
00:05:01,899 --> 00:05:03,999
This is the longest day in Northern

114
00:05:04,079 --> 00:05:07,534
Hemisphere and hence it is called 'Summer

115
00:05:07,626 --> 00:05:09,659
Solstice', while in the Southern Hemisphere,

116
00:05:09,739 --> 00:05:11,199
it is the shortest day.

117
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:14,480
Let's Learn More.

118
00:05:17,340 --> 00:05:19,820
Earth keeps rotating due to inertia,

119
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:23,120
the same reason you continue moving forward

120
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:25,060
when you stop a bike suddenly.

121
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:28,600
This movement doesn’t stop because there’s no

122
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:30,620
friction in space to slow it down!

123
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,200
What is Equinox and When Does It

124
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:35,600
Occur?

125
00:05:38,060 --> 00:05:40,640
The sun falls directly on the equator

126
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:42,060
two times in a year.

127
00:05:42,760 --> 00:05:45,260
During this period there is equal length

128
00:05:45,340 --> 00:05:47,280
of day and night all over the

129
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:47,680
world.

130
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:49,380
In Northern Hemisphere,

131
00:05:49,840 --> 00:05:52,280
the March Equinox is called the Vernal

132
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:55,960
or Spring Equinox while September Equinox is

133
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:57,580
called Autumnal Equinox.

134
00:05:57,660 --> 00:06:02,200
Spring Equinox (March 21st) marks the beginning

135
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:02,940
of spring.

136
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:07,560
Autumn Equinox (September 23rd) marks the beginning

137
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:08,360
of autumn.

138
00:06:10,660 --> 00:06:11,120
Recall.

139
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:15,120
The Earth's movements,

140
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:17,400
rotation and revolution,

141
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:20,260
have significant affects on our lives.

142
00:06:21,620 --> 00:06:23,200
Rotation causes day and night,

143
00:06:23,780 --> 00:06:26,180
while revolution leads to the change of

144
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:26,600
seasons.

145
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:30,660
Solstices and equinoxes mark the shift in

146
00:06:30,740 --> 00:06:33,520
seasons, playing an essential role in our

147
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:34,980
climate and timekeeping.

148
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:38,360
Let's Remember.

149
00:06:41,020 --> 00:06:43,020
The Earth moves in two ways:

150
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:45,320
rotation and revolution.

151
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:48,220
Rotation causes day and night,

152
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:50,620
while revolution causes seasons.

153
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:54,460
The Earth completes one rotation in 24

154
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:57,971
hours and one revolution in three hundred

155
00:06:58,051 --> 00:06:59,840
and sixty-five and one quarter days.

156
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:03,260
Solstices occur in June and December,

157
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:05,980
marking the longest and shortest days.

158
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:09,460
Equinoxes occur in March and September,

159
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:11,840
when day and night are equal.

160
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:14,800
Word Bank.

161
00:07:17,900 --> 00:07:20,360
Rotation – Spinning of the Earth on

162
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:21,100
its axis.

163
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:25,220
Revolution – Movement of the Earth around

164
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:25,740
the Sun.

165
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:28,840
Orbit – The path of the Earth

166
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:30,040
around the Sun.

167
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:33,040
Solstice – When the Sun is at

168
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:35,520
its farthest point north or south.

169
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:39,000
Equinox – When day and night are

170
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:39,600
equal.
